/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - For VGS below VT a few electrons still sit at the surface, their number set by a Boltzmann factor.
   - ID = IVT · 10(VGS − VT)/SS · (1 − e−VDS/φt)
   - IVT is the current at VGS = VT for the given W/L (it scales with W/L); φt = kT/q is the thermal voltage, 26 mV at 300 K; SS is the subthreshold swing, below.
   - The thermal voltage is written φt here so that VT always means the threshold voltage.
   - The subthreshold swing is the gate voltage needed to change the current tenfold:
   - SS = 2.3·n·φt, with n = 1 + Cdep/Cox
   - 2.3 = ln 10; n is the body factor, 1.2 to 1.5 in a bulk device, because the depletion capacitance Cdep shares the gate voltage with the oxide.
   - The off current Ioff is the current at VGS = 0 and VDS = VDD, quoted per µm of width: Ioff = IVT·10−VT/SS.
   - Static power is VDD × total leakage.
*/
