/* book Worked example: Q: A process has SS = 80 mV/decade and Ioff = 10 nA/µm with VT = 0.3 V. A designer raises VT by 100 mV. (a) By what factor does Ioff fall? (b) What is the new Ioff? (c) A block has 10 mm of total off-transistor width at VDD = 1 V; find its leakage current and static power before and after. (d) Find n, with φt = 26 mV.
   1. (a) Factor = 10100/80 = 101.25 = 17.8.
   2. (b) Ioff = 10/17.8 = 0.562 nA/µm.
   3. (c) W = 10 mm = 10⁴ µm. Before: 10 nA/µm × 10⁴ µm = 100 µA, so 100 µW at 1 V. After: 0.562 × 10⁴ = 5.62 µA, so 5.6 µW.
   4. (d) n = SS/(2.3φt) = 80/(2.3 × 26) = 1.34.
   Answer: Leakage falls 17.8 times, to 0.56 nA/µm; the block leaks 5.6 µA (5.6 µW) instead of 100 µA (100 µW); n = 1.34. */
