/* book Worked example 2: Q: For the original device (SS = 80 mV/decade at 300 K, VT = 0.3 V), the chip heats to 360 K. SS grows in proportion to T and VT falls by 1.5 mV/K. By what factor does Ioff grow?
   1. SS at 360 K = 80 × 360/300 = 96 mV/decade.
   2. VT at 360 K = 0.3 − 1.5 × 10⁻³ × 60 = 0.21 V.
   3. Ioff ∝ 10−VT/SS: at 300 K, 10−0.300/0.080 = 10−3.75 = 1.78 × 10⁻⁴; at 360 K, 10−0.210/0.096 = 10−2.19 = 6.49 × 10⁻³.
   4. Ratio = 6.49 × 10⁻³ / 1.78 × 10⁻⁴ = 36.5 (taking IVT as constant).
   Answer: Ioff grows about 36 times, from 10 nA/µm to about 365 nA/µm, for a 60 K rise. */
