/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - In a short planar device, field lines from the drain reach the source end of the channel through the body underneath, lowering the barrier (DIBL) and raising Ioff.
   - The better fix is a thin body.
   - The fin is a narrow ridge of silicon, of width Wfin and height Hfin, etched from the wafer.
   - Weff = 2Hfin + Wfin per fin (tri-gate); Weff = 2Hfin (double gate)
   - Because the body is so thin, it is left undoped or lightly doped.
   - A planar designer can draw any W.
   - At the newest nodes the fin gives way to gate-all-around (GAA) nanosheets: horizontal sheets of silicon stacked vertically with the gate on all four sides, whose width can again be chosen.
*/
