/* book Worked example: Q: A tri-gate FinFET has Wfin = 10 nm and Hfin = 30 nm. (a) Find Weff per fin. (b) How many fins give at least 700 nm of width? (c) The process gives 1 mA per µm of effective width; find the current per fin and in total. (d) How many fins are needed for 720 nm?
   1. (a) Weff = 2 × 30 + 10 = 70 nm.
   2. (b) 700/70 = 10 fins exactly.
   3. (c) 70 nm = 0.07 µm, so 0.07 × 1 mA = 70 µA per fin; 10 fins give 0.70 mA.
   4. (d) 720/70 = 10.3, so 11 fins (770 nm): widths come in whole fins only.
   Answer: Weff = 70 nm; 10 fins for 700 nm carrying 70 µA each, 0.7 mA in total; 11 fins for 720 nm. */
